WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.001
The finished project: a narrated video with moving images, captions and a look.

00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:07.716
Shorts: vertical clips picked from the video, each with its own title and hashtags.

00:00:07.716 --> 00:00:11.427
The YouTube description with chapter timestamps, hashtags and tags, ready to copy.

00:00:11.427 --> 00:00:13.633
The article in a reading view, with contents and search.

00:00:13.633 --> 00:00:15.840
Narration in your own voice, every piece levelled to one loudness.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.048
The images and the thumbnail, from your own prompts. Redo any one of them.

00:00:18.048 --> 00:00:19.855
A PDF of the article, with a cover, contents and a theme of your own.

00:00:19.855 --> 00:00:22.055
Run cost: what the run cost per stage and model.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:25.493
Checkpoints to approve work before it moves on, and a history of every version.

00:00:25.493 --> 00:00:28.003
Several voices: a podcast, audiobook, radio drama or interview, with a voice per speaker.

00:00:28.003 --> 00:00:34.750
Play: pick a template, type the topic, see the look before you start.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.168
Cuts that follow the narration, transitions, a colour grade, grain and chapter cards.

00:00:38.168 --> 00:00:40.781
Automatic reviews: a reviewer model checks each stage and sends work back.

00:00:40.781 --> 00:00:42.992
The Library: prompts written once with {{keywords}}, templates and starter packs.

00:00:42.992 --> 00:00:45.200
Channels: a brand kit, a series brief, templates and a cast for each channel.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:48.009
The calendar: a schedule works through its queued topics, one run each.

00:00:48.009 --> 00:00:51.030
Prepare upload: every file and text in the order YouTube Studio asks for them.

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:53.266
Ctrl+K for everything: regenerate, copy, prepare upload, start a video.
